## Conclusion

DCGM's "DCP" module (Device Client Profiling — the piece that actually watches and reports field
values) never loads on this RTX 4070 + WSL2 driver stack ("This request is serviced by a module of
DCGM that is not currently loaded"), independent of container capabilities. The exporter falls back
to its default-counters.csv field list but still returns zero metrics (HTTP 200, empty body) because
none of those fields resolve either. This is a known class of limitation, not a misconfiguration on
this machine: DCGM's field-watching stack targets datacenter GPUs and/or bare-metal Linux driver
installs; consumer GeForce cards and WSL2's virtualized GPU passthrough are both outside what it
fully supports. Container removed after the test (`docker rm -f dcgm-exporter`) — no resources left
running.
